  "slug": "protein-network-cd75",
  "summary": "General-purpose LLMs and multimodal inverse folding now extend protein design beyond sequence-only conditioning.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is protein design conditioned on learned sequence models and evolutionary or structural context. The MSA-Transformer iteratively generates hybrid sequences between homologous source and target proteins, tracing feature inheritance. ABACUS-T combines sidechains, ligands, a protein language model, multiple backbone states and MSA evolution in multimodal inverse folding to redesign functional proteins. The general-purpose LLM DeepSeek V3.2 is tested for 4-helix bundle sequences and solubility-improving mutants, validated via pLDDT and RMSD. BinderFlow automates end-to-end de novo binder design in a modular pipeline with campaign monitoring, while Martinize2 and Vermouth address coarse-grained topology generation, a supporting rather than design-centred step. What is new is the breadth of conditioning and the evaluation of general-purpose LLMs as protein designers.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
